                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "237518743",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198046776516",
                            "num_reviews": 167,
                            "playtime_forever": 182,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 182,
                            "last_played": 1791773809
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This is one of those games I've had in my inventory since... Dec 2015. I'm trying to rest my left arm from a stress injury and am going through some old point and click games so I decided to finally play this. I'm glad I did, I ended up really enjoying it. The story was a bit...vague on some details but horrifying on others. I was genuinely creeped out a couple times. Its got its flaws for sure, its short and the 'puzzles' are pretty limited but at least I didn't get stuck. Also I'm pretty sure one puzzle is just in there to poke fun at the usual 'moon logic' of this genre. The art is lovely, just the perfect kind of pixel art. Its pretty short, with only the 3 chapters. Supposedly there is a sequel to come? But it was promised in 2016 and it seems the dev has been having health issues. Hopefully they are doing well, I would love another game, but health takes priority. anyway, I liked it for what it is, a simple and quick point & click.",
